From b62d68760c2d67e4606220b69e20ee0fb8fe5f77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Overholtz <mike.n.va@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:17:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SPRINT A: idempotent scanning with schema v11, natural keys,
 and end-of-scan reconciliation

Schema v11 (MigrationRunner):
- IsActive tombstones on Artists/Releases/Models/Files; SourcePipeline
  lineage on Models/Releases; real ContentHash column on Files
- One-time migration retires legacy v1 rows (FolderPath IS NULL is the
  lineage marker), dedupes pre-v11 duplicate Models per FolderPath
  (keeps newest), and enforces UX_Models_FolderPath (unique among
  active rows) + IX_Files_ContentHash partial indexes

Scanner (DirectoryScannerService):
- Tier 3 upsert keyed on the natural key FolderPath: model GUIDs survive
  re-scans and user metadata (IsFavorite, PrintNotes) is preserved
- Per-release transactions with per-release error isolation
- Real content hashing (SHA-256 with edge sampling) replaces the
  path+size placeholder hash; quick-hash fallback on IO errors
- End-of-scan reconciliation sweep retires Files/Models/Releases/
  Artists whose folders vanished from disk, scoped to the scan root
  with separator-boundary checks, skipped on cancelled scans
- Reactivates retired artists/releases/models on rescan

Read side:
- Catalog, release, and detail queries filter on IsActive so retired
  rows never surface in the UI
- Dashboard status text reports retired counts

Tests: 18-test regression suite covering rescan idempotency, identity
and metadata preservation, reconciliation (file/model/release/artist),
root scoping, cancellation safety, content hashing, and the v10->v11
migration (legacy retirement, dedup, unique index).

Co-authored-by: Perplexity <noreply@perplexity.ai>
